WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.660
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:05.640
Can you find the total area of the red spots?

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:11.080
The diagram involves a rectangle with dimensions 10 and 20

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.080
The rectangle has one of its diagonals connected.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:23.660
Inside the rectangle are two circles of equal size wich are tangent to each other and tangent to the rectangle.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.100
If you can solve this problem,

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.560
then try this much harder variation.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.780
This was supposedly asked to sixth
graders in China.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:38.820
Can you now find the total area of the
red spots?

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:43.680
Give these problems a try and when you're ready keep watching the video for the solution.

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:49.140
We will get started on the first problem.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:53.039
We will solve for the
area of the red regions by subtraction.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:58.700
We will take the area of this triangle and
then we'll subtract out

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.379
different portions of the circles.

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:06.960
So we can set up a formula that the area
of the red regions is equal to the area

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.790
of this right triangle

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:14.410
minus the area of each of these pieces from
the different circles.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:20.280
Now it looks like these two pieces actually join to form
one circle.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:27.820
You can notice this by symmetry and I will illustrate it by
putting these two pieces together.

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:34.100
We now solve for the area of each piece.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:39.500
The area of a right triangle is its base times its height divided by two.

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:43.500
The area of a circle is PI times r
squared.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:48.580
The right triangle has a base of 20 and a height of 10.

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:55.080
The circle has a radius which is equal
to half the height of the rectangle

00:01:55.340 --> 00:02:02.580
and it's radius is equal to five, so the
circle has an area of pi times 5 squared.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:06.980
This means the area of the red regions
is equal to 100

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:12.560
minus 25 pi, or approximately 21.46

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:17.940
Now let's tackle the second part of the
problem.

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:24.620
We know the area of the red regions as
illustrated is a hundred minus 25 pi.

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:31.100
The second part says what would happen
if you remove this region from the lower

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:32.630
left hand corner,

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:40.300
so we can solve for the red regions by solving for the area of this particular piece.

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:46.220
To do that we'll
consider a simplified diagram we'll just

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:51.430
consider one of the circles and it will
be inside of a square,

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:53.880
with side length 10.

00:02:57.380 --> 00:03:00.080
We can again solve this by
subtraction.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:02.640
We consider this right triangle

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:08.000
We're going to remove this portion from
the lower right hand corner

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:11.720
and then we're going to remove this portion of the circle

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:16.660
and what remains is the area of the lower left hand corner.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:20.880
So we'll set up our formula that the
area we want is equal

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:23.880
to the area of the rec- of the triangle

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:28.440
minus the area of this piece in the lower
right hand corner

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:31.400
minus this piece of the circle.

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:38.560
The area of the right triangle is its base times its height divided by 2

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.280
This right triangle has a
height of 5

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:46.000
so its area will be 10 times 5 divided by 2

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:50.280
What about the piece in the lower right hand corner?

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:56.700
We can solve this by subtraction. We'll consider one quarter of the square.

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:01.340
This square has a side length of five.

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:06.510
We then subtract out one quarter of the
circle.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:13.660
So we can solve for this piece by taking one quarter of the square and subtracting out one quarter of the circle.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:18.800
This square has a side length of
5 so it's area is 25

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:21.640
The circle has a radius of 5,

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:26.180
so one quarter of the circle, is PI times 5
squared divided by 4

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:33.280
So we solve for this portion is 25 times 1 minus PI over 4

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:36.080
So we just have one more piece to solve for.

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:39.060
This is the most complicated
part.

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:41.920
We'll again consider it by subtraction.

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:45.340
We'll consider this sector of the circle

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:52.420
We'll then remove out this isosceles triangle and that'll leave us the area of the piece we want.

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:58.520
So we can again set up a formula that
the region we want is equal to the area

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:00.630
of a sector of the circle

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:04.010
minus the area of this isosceles triangle.

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:11.360
In order to calculate these areas we're going to have to use formulas for these
particular shapes.

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:17.820
If we have a circle with radius of R
and a sector

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:22.160
having an angle alpha and this is in radians,

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:27.880
then the area of the sector is equal to
R squared times alpha divided by 2

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:36.360
For triangle with side lengths A, B and an angle in between them of beta

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:41.880
It's area is equal to A times B times
the SIN of beta divided by 2

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:44.520
So,

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:49.560
we now need to consider what are the angles involved and what are the lenghts  involved in these formulas.

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:55.620
Well the circle has a radius which is one-half of the square which is this a length of 10

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:59.720
So the radius is 5 and the radius is 5
over here too.

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:03.940
This is also the other side of the triangle so we have an isosceles triangle.

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:12.380
If we consider the right triangle from the lower left hand corner and say this has an angle of theta,

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:19.000
the radius of the circle will be parallel to the side of the rectangle.

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:22.920
So its corresponding angle over here will also be theta.

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:27.920
The other side of this triangle
we have an isosceles triangle so it will

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:29.910
also have an angle theta.

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:37.260
This means the central angle of this sector (will be 2 PI-) will be PI minus 2 theta.

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:41.360
Because the angles in a triangle
add up to PI radians.

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:47.380
So we can now substitute in these dimensions into our formulas.

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:53.420
We can simplify the formula for SIN of PI minus 2 theta

00:06:53.420 --> 00:06:57.220
because SIN of PI  minus 2 theta is equal to sine of two theta.

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:02.000
SIN of PI minus any angle is
equal to SIN of that angle.

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:05.440
So now we need to consider what is this
angle theta.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:11.180
Well in our original triangle it has a
base- it has a height of 5 and a base of 10

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:14.520
So we can use trigonometry to say,

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:18.900
that the angle theta is equal to the inverse
tangent of five over 10

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:21.180
which is the inverse tangent of one half.

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:24.660
So we can substitute that in

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:27.780
and we'll simplify your formula for the area of the sector.

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:30.720
Now for the area of the isosceles triangle

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:34.360
We can use the double angle
formula for SIN of two theta

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:36.200
and simplify that a bit

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:40.240
and now we need to solve for the sine of theta and the cosine of theta.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:43.220
Well in this right triangle

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:46.320
we have one side length 10 and a height
of 5

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:49.100
So we  know that its diagonal can be

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:53.160
solved by the Pythagorean theorem, so we have a (hun-) 10 squared which is a 100

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:55.040
plus 5 squared which is 25

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:56.280
So that means

00:07:56.800 --> 00:08:01.240
the square root of these is (eq-) the sum of these is equal to the length of the hypotenuse

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:04.440
so with the hypotenuse is equal to the square root of a 125

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:09.840
So we can solve for the SIN of theta is
5 divided by the square root of a 125

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:14.040
and the COS of theta is equal to 10 divided by the square root of a 125

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:16.860
So substituting that in and simplifying,

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:20.740
we end up with the area of the isosceles is triangle is equal to 10

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:25.560
And now we have a formula for the region of the circle that we want.

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:29.960
It's 25 PI over 2 minus 25

00:08:29.969 --> 00:08:32.529
the inverse tangent of one half minus 10

00:08:32.969 --> 00:08:36.839
So we have all the different areas of
the pieces we want and we can simplify

00:08:36.839 --> 00:08:43.649
this formula to get the area of the
lower left hand corner is equal to 10 minus

00:08:43.649 --> 00:08:48.529
20 5 PI over 4 plus 25 times the inverse
tangent of one half.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:51.500
So we will put this all together.

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:54.940
This is approximately 1.956

00:08:55.860 --> 00:09:00.480
So now we're going to put this all together and we can calculate the area of the red regions.

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:04.920
So as illustrated the
red regions are a 100 minus 25 PI

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:10.360
In our second problem we want to remove
this one piece in the lower left-hand corner

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:11.980
which we just solved for.

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:17.300
So we can substitute that in our formula
and then simplify to get the area of

00:09:17.310 --> 00:09:23.069
these red regions is a 90 minus 18.75 PI minus 25 times the inverse

00:09:23.069 --> 00:09:28.709
tangent of one-half and this is approximately 19.504

